<div class="ff-guide-topics" aria-label="Part selection guide topics">
  <details class="ff-guide-topic" id="replacement-checklist" data-ff-guide{% if open_checklist %} open{% endif %}>
    <summary>Replacement checklist</summary>
    <div class="rte ff-guide-body">
      <p>Compare the part on your instrument with the exact replacement variant's drawings and specifications before ordering.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Identify the part.</strong> Record the instrument model, the existing part's markings, and its orientation. A similar outline does not establish compatibility.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare the mounting.</strong> Check every screw, pin, post, bushing and mounting hole, together with the space available around and below the part.</li>
        <li><strong>Record the measurements.</strong> Use the same units and reference points on the original part and the replacement drawing.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the specification.</strong> Confirm the required pieces, hardware, wiring and electrical values where relevant. Check what is included with the selected variant.</li>
        <li><strong>Resolve any mismatch first.</strong> If a dimension or mounting detail is missing, confirm it before ordering or modifying the instrument.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>By component</h3>
      <p><strong>Tuning machines:</strong> compare the headstock hole, bushing diameter, post height, rear screw or pin positions, and left/right orientation.</p>
      <p><strong>Bridges and tailpieces:</strong> compare mounting centres, outside string spacing, height, footprint and available cavity depth.</p>
      <p><strong>Pickups and electronics:</strong> compare the footprint, mounting ears, pole spacing, shaft dimensions, terminals and wiring requirements.</p>
      <p><strong>Pickguards and small hardware:</strong> compare the complete outline, cutouts, every screw position, bore size, shaft shape and thread specification.</p>
      <p><a href="#measurement-guide">Read the measurement guide</a> · <a href="#finish-guide">Compare hardware finishes</a></p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="ff-guide-topic" id="measurement-guide" data-ff-guide>
    <summary>Measuring replacement parts</summary>
    <div class="rte ff-guide-body">
      <p>Start with the original part and the measured drawing for the exact replacement variant. Record each measurement rather than estimating fit from a photograph.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Use consistent units.</strong> Keep millimetres and inches clearly labelled. Measure both parts from the same reference points.</li>
        <li><strong>Separate the spacing measurements.</strong> String spacing, mounting post spacing and screw hole spacing describe different features. Measure centre to centre where the drawing specifies centres.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the full envelope.</strong> Record width, length, height and the depth needed below the mounting surface. Allow for moving parts and nearby components.</li>
        <li><strong>Check every fixing.</strong> Compare hole diameters, bushing or post sizes, screw or pin locations, and thread specifications.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Bridge string spacing:</strong> E-to-E is the distance between the centres of the two outside strings (E-to-E). Do not substitute that distance for the mounting post or screw spacing.</p>
      <p>Do not infer thread pitch or electrical specifications from appearance. Use the product's stated specification, and confirm any missing values before installation.</p>
      <p><a href="#replacement-checklist">Return to the replacement checklist</a></p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="ff-guide-topic" id="finish-guide" data-ff-guide>
    <summary>Comparing hardware finishes</summary>
    <div class="rte ff-guide-body">
      <p>Compare the finish name and photographs for the exact product variant. A finish choice does not change the need to check fit, dimensions and mounting details.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Check the variant label.</strong> Chrome, nickel, black and gold are finish descriptions; do not assume two products with a similar colour have the same material or coating.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare under similar lighting.</strong> Lighting, reflections, screens and the condition of existing hardware can change the apparent colour. The swatches on the homepage are illustrative.</li>
        <li><strong>Match the complete set.</strong> Compare screws, bushings, knobs and other visible pieces as well as the main component. Check which pieces are included.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirm care requirements.</strong> Follow the finish-specific care information supplied with the product rather than assuming every surface accepts the same cleaner or polish.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If an exact visual match matters, confirm the selected finish against the existing hardware before ordering.</p>
      <p><a href="#replacement-checklist">Return to the replacement checklist</a></p>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
